{
  "_doc": "Every sound the game makes, as a synthesis recipe (autoload/sound.gd builds each once, the first time it plays). A sound is a list of layers mixed together; each layer: wave (sine, square, saw, triangle, noise), freq and freq_end in Hz (a glide), dur and delay in seconds, attack and release (seconds of fade in and out), gain, lowpass (Hz, softens saw, square and noise), vibrato [rate Hz, depth as a share of pitch], tremolo [rate Hz, depth 0..1], repeat [count, gap seconds]. A real recording can replace any recipe later: give the event a \"file\" (res://...) instead of layers (a \"loop\" one loops; \"bus\" puts a loop on another bus, Ambience for the farm's sounds; \"always\": never refused by the cap on loops, the weather's own). pitch_jitter varies the pitch a little each time so repeats don't sound mechanical. An effect is under 2 s; one marked \"long\" (thunder rolling) may run 5 s. A recording can also come in takes: \"files\" (a list); each play picks one, never the same twice running. Recordings are cut from CC0 downloads by tools/sound_cuts/make_sounds.py, or made from scratch by make_generated.py (art/sound/SOURCES.md). voices: each animal family's call; young_voices: a baby's own call (a family without one uses the adult's, higher: Sound.YOUNG_PITCH); voice_pitch: a family's (or an item's) call played lower or higher.",
